From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:06:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 037/104] clk: samsung: add Exynos7570 clock controller (MIF,
 FSYS, PERI)

Add the CMU_MIF, CMU_FSYS and CMU_PERI clock controllers of the Exynos7570
SoC: the three shared PLLs with their muxes, the CLKCMU mux/divider/gate
chains feeding FSYS and PERI, the bus clocks, and the gates needed by the
eMMC and SD controllers, the USB DRD, the UART/USI/SPI/I2C blocks, the MCT,
the watchdog, the RTC and the GPIO blocks.

Unlike the Exynos7870, the 7570 CMUs use one CLK_CON_MUX/CLK_CON_DIV register
per mux/divider and grouped CLK_ENABLE registers for the gates, so the 7870
driver cannot be reused. The register layout, bit positions and parents
follow the downstream pwrcal tables. Muxes are modelled by their select
field only; the per-mux enable bit is left as the bootloader set it.

The USB20 PHY core clock comes from a handshake-controlled 20 MHz USB PLL.
Only its rate is represented for now.

Add the matching devicetree binding and the CMU nodes.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit a0da14c13439ec1b35b09704d69387f632e65162)
